WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Type II is the bread and butter of residential HVAC. This is what you'll use
every day.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Leak detection methods: electronic leak detectors sense refrigerant vapor and
alarm when concentration exceeds the threshold. UV dye is injected into the
system and glows under UV light at the leak location. Soap bubbles applied to

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Electronic Leak Detector: Senses refrigerant vapor concentration. Must be
calibrated before each use.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Standing Pressure Test: System pressurized with nitrogen overnight. Pressure
drop indicates a leak.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Finding leaks is one of the most
time-consuming parts of HVAC service. Mastering multiple detection methods makes
you more efficient.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Calibrate electronic detectors before each use. And — Never
